      <title>Squeak 2.26.3</title>
      <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:04:55 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>22603</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.26.3</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>Chat polish: earlier turns no longer redraw when only the newest one changes, long commands shorten in the middle, durations keep their width as they tick, long command output stops at 12 lines with Show all, and steps read their duration and open state to VoiceOver.</li><li>A reply being written re-parses only its last block, so long replies stay smooth as they stream; teammates' names stay on one line and read "From ...".</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.26.2</h4><ul><li>Multiplayer: members can message and answer shared threads and run their own agents, shown as "Powered by ... · Flotilla".</li><li>The owner controls what each member may do, and what each thread allows, from the People menu and the thread's lock menu.</li><li>Changes apply live, without restarting a thread.</li><li>Replies to Claude/Codex running in Terminal now come with the external add-ons.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.26.1</h4><ul><li>The chat is rebuilt: a new message never shows old work, steps only grow in place, the view stays where you left it, and shared threads show everyone's messages in one order.</li><li>A stream keeps its tabs: going Home and back no longer drops thread tabs, and opening an older thread from the Dashboard, a search or a notification adds a tab beside the others instead of replacing them. Each stream's tabs also survive a relaunch.</li><li>A Markdown file (.md, .markdown, .mdx) opens as a rendered preview with a Preview | Source switch in its header: headings, lists, task lists, tables, code with Copy, quotes and images next to the file. Edit switches to the source and Done returns to your last pick.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
